# NET-REMOTE: a remote (simulated-proxy) pawn as another player sees it. The server's pawn prefab is read off the
# frame (unread shell + AsyncAssetLoader request) and its dependency closure requested when that read lands; pawn
# spawns wait for both (no sync load). The remote pawn is interpolated on a snapshot buffer (delay = arrival jitter
# p95 + one interval) and casts its skinned shadow; GpuScene latches PrevLocalToWorld once per frame.
# Played by scripts/Dev/net_scenario.py (NET-SCENARIO-PLAY): DesertServer --role all sending with 75 ms lag + 30 ms
# jitter + 2 % loss, Editor B = observer (player 1, its own pawn camera, every frame shot), bot A (player 2) walking a
# 400 cm shuttle 5 m in front of B (probe --waypoints, steered from the server position). B joins first, A once B
# is in session (B spawns standing at -421 on WP_Protocol's hill), so the spawn points are listed in admission order.
# |dir| 0.02 moves A ~6 cm per wall second: the remote pawn is interpolated on the network's wall clock.
# Pass history (p5-p10, run_net5b.sh): git log of this file.
Мир Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
# The spawn points are the ground (feet, cm): (0, 650) is -421 (the placer: floor 121 cm under (0, -300, 650), NET-INPUT-PACK
# scn-1127-073438 server.log; B rests at -421, NET-REMOTE scn-1126-155428 A.log); (0, 150) is -464 from the WP_Protocol landscape tile samples (h=(s-32768)/128*ZScale 4, 200 cm spacing; reproduces every placer reading).
Роль server server lag=75 jitter=30 loss=2 --role all --source 0,0,0 --pawn assets:Prefabs/Pawn_Player.deprefab --spawn 0,-421,650 --spawn 0,-464,150 --steps 1000000
Ждать server 60 \[Server\] listening on port
Роль B editor account=1 lag=75 loss=2 --play --shot-frames 100000 --shot-every 1 --shot-player-view --quality PostProcess.MotionBlurQuality=0
Ждать B 1800 \[Net\] in session
Ждать B 600 drawn own \(-?0,-4\d\d,650\)
# Когда: A walks the shuttle across B's view (B's pawn camera faces -Z at the segment's middle).
Роль A bot account=2 lag=75 loss=2 --seconds 15000 --waypoints "-200,-440,150;200,-440,150" --dir 0.02,0,0 --hold-actions 4 --hold-from 6 --hold-until 10
Ждать B 120 \[Net\] remote pawn net id \d+ \(player \d+\) spawned
# [pawn_mannequin_proxy] the bot holds IA_Crouch (mask 4 = PawnActions bit 2) from 6 s to 10 s of its run; the server
# replicates the crouched mode bit, B's WriteMoveState sets IsCrouched, Mannequin_Locomotion enters Crouch. Shot first, while
# A is still before 6 s: `fresh` on A takes only this run's crouch-start line as it is logged (an already-logged line times
# out instead of shooting outside the window); `fresh` on B skips B's lines logged during that wait, so the shot is 2 B
# reports (~2 s, well over lag + interpolation delay) after the crouch starts and before it ends at 10 s.
Ждать A 60 fresh \] actions 4 at
Ждать B 30 fresh 2x \[Net\] t=
Тогда B pawn_mannequin_proxy B's view inside the bot's crouch window: A walks crouched (pelvis visibly lower, knees bent, crouch-walk step), facing its walk, its feet on the ground - not sunk, not hanging; no capsule anywhere
Ждать B 60 3x \[Net\] t=
Тогда B net5_remote_walk1 B's view: A as one solid mannequin (grey body, dark joints, head, arms, legs) on the slope 5 m ahead, walking FACING the waypoint it walks to, its feet on the ground (none sunk, none hanging), not in a jump pose; its shadow at its feet; no ghost, no trail
Ждать B 60 5x \[Net\] t=
Тогда B net5_remote_walk2 A a few cm further along the shuttle, still one solid mannequin facing its walk, feet on the ground, not in a jump pose, its shadow at its feet; no stray shadow elsewhere
Ждать B 60 5x \[Net\] t=
Тогда B net5_remote_walk3 A further along again, same: solid mannequin facing its walk, feet on the ground, not in a jump pose, shadow at its feet, no ghost/trail
# Тогда [net5_remote_shadow]: interpolation delay 100-200 ms, 0 snaps.
Ждать B 30 \[Net\] interpolation buffer: delay 1\d\d ms .*\(0 snap\(s\)\)
Нет B \(([1-9]\d*) snap\(s\)\)
